      {
        "thread_id": "TH1",
        "thread_goal": "Align on current loading, stacking and cleaning practices and main pain points.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 18289,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Team, let's kick off the Warehouse Loading Bay Safety and Efficiency Upgrade project. To start, let's map out how things are done today. Can everyone share their view on the current loading, stacking, and cleaning steps? This will help us with T1.",
            "mentions": [
              27041,
              40035,
              72769,
              366315
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 27041,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Right now it's mostly about speed. Grab the pallet, get it on the truck, move to the next one. Stacking is just 'heavy stuff on the bottom'.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 40035,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "Pretty much. There's no standard way, it depends who is on shift. Sometimes pallets are staged, sometimes it's a rush to pull them from the racks. It causes delays when you have to re-shuffle things.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 72769,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "From the cleaning side, it's supposed to be done at the end of the shift, but if we're running late, it gets rushed or skipped. Spills are sometimes just left for the next shift to find.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "eyes",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 366315,
            "reply_to": "M4",
            "text": "Exactly. And empty pallets or shrink wrap are often left in the staging area, which you have to clear before you can even start loading.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M6",
            "speaker_id": 18289,
            "reply_to": "M5",
            "text": "Okay, so key issues are: inconsistent loading process, no standard stacking rules, and rushed/skipped cleaning. Thanks all. To make this manageable, which routes or load types give us the most trouble?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M7",
            "speaker_id": 27041,
            "reply_to": "M6",
            "text": "The City Loop route is always a pain, so many stops.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M8",
            "speaker_id": 40035,
            "reply_to": "M7",
            "text": "The City Loop is frequent, but the loads are usually uniform. I think the Industrial Park route is a bigger problem. It's always mixed loads - heavy machinery parts, chemical drums, standard pallets. That's where stacking gets dangerous.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M9",
            "speaker_id": 72769,
            "reply_to": "M8",
            "text": "I agree. The Industrial Park trucks are the ones that come back with shifted loads. Focusing there would have the biggest safety impact.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M10",
            "speaker_id": 18289,
            "reply_to": "M9",
            "text": "That's a strong point. Let's propose a focus then. We'll target the Industrial Park route and mixed pallet/special container loads for the first draft of the new procedures.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M11",
            "speaker_id": 366315,
            "reply_to": "M10",
            "text": "That makes sense. It covers the most variables.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M12",
            "speaker_id": 40035,
            "reply_to": "M10",
            "text": "I'm on board with that.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M13",
            "speaker_id": 27041,
            "reply_to": "M10",
            "text": "ok sounds good",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M14",
            "speaker_id": 18289,
            "reply_to": "M13",
            "text": "Great, we have an agreement. D1: We will focus on the Industrial Park route and its typical mixed loads for the new procedures first. I'll start mapping the current process for that as the main part of T1.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1"
